tools.description:
Create a workspace, the place pods, storage, tasks and servings live in. An empty workspace costs nothing;
        what runs in it is billed as usual. `name` is optional (at most 63 characters) and must differ from the names of
        all the user's workspaces; omit it to get a generated name like

Show money movements: `kind` "credit" lists top-ups and refunds; "earnings" shows host earnings per day;
        "payouts" lists the payouts of a host's earnings (the last 90 days by default), with a `summary` of the payout
        account: whether it exists and is fully onboarded, and the earnings

Delete a storage volume and all data on it. `storage` is its pv_name or display name from the storages tool.
        With confirm=false (default) it only returns what would be deleted (including pods that still mount it);
        call again with confirm=true after the user agreed. Volumes mounted by

Pause (paused=true) or resume (paused=false) a serving. Paused servings stop billing and stop answering requests.
        Resuming restarts billing, so paused=false with confirm=false (default) only returns the serving's current state;
        call again with confirm=true after the user agreed. Paus

Delete a serving and its endpoint. With confirm=false (default) it only returns the serving's current state;
        call again with confirm=true after the user agreed.
